There seems to be a lot of interest in this little one, so I am posting
it.  Cchk is a program which checks your C code for suspicious
practices.  It checks indentation (not always to my taste, but mostly),
particularly for matching {} pairs (the indentation of the line with the
closer must match that of the line with the opener), and if-else
matches.  Also looks for if ( a = b ) constructs, and nested comments.
I like it, anyway.

=Spencer

